spans.s:
√paṇ (páṇati, -te; paṇitá).
 —1. bargain;
buy;
 —2. bet, wage, stake, play. [prob.
for *paln: cf. πέρνημι and πωλέω, ‘sell’;
Ger. feil, ‘for sale, venal.’]
+ ā, in āpaṇa, ‘market.’
+ vi, sell.

paṇa, m.
 —1. bargain, stipulation, 45^14;
 —2. wage, gage, prize;
 —3. a certain
coin, 47^16. [√paṇ.]
